      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_07cc2afb",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: urinal_cake_meme; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The meme depicts a urinal cake with the text 'who decided to call this a urinal cake instead of a piscuit,' using a pun to mock the object's appearance. The humor is derived from the visual resemblance to a biscuit or cookie, which is a harmless, non-offensive joke. There is no toxicity, hate, or harmful content present, as it does not target any protected group or promote harm. The intent is purely comedic and based on wordplay and visual analogy, not on disparaging any community or individual.",
