    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_3b65acbc",
      "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
      "instance_name": "mapping_1",
      "label": "urinal cake is humorously mapped to a biscuit",
      "description": "The text 'who decided to call this a urinal cake instead of a piscuit' creates an analogical mapping where the visual entity 'urinal_cake' is being humorously compared to a 'biscuit' (via the pun 'piscuit'). The meme's humor relies on the visual resemblance of the urinal cake to a biscuit, which is the core of the analogical mapping. The text explicitly questions the naming, implying the object visually resembles a biscuit, thus mapping the visual entity to the textual concept of a biscuit.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
